From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jassim Shanavaskhan <jshanava@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: add and fix STA AssociatedDevice parameters

Add new AssociatedDevice DM parameters and fix existing ones.
All are populated at AP-STA-CONNECTED event after pAD->object
is created by wld_vap_sync_device.

New parameters:
  Channel        - AP radio channel (pAP->pRadio->channel)
  OperatingClass - AP radio operating class (WiFi.Radio.N.OperatingClass)
  LinkBandwidth  - AP radio bandwidth (pRadio->runningChannelBandwidth)
  ERP            - STA ERP flag from 802.11 capability field
  MinTxPower     - STA minimum TX power from 802.11 Power Capability IE
  MaxTxPower     - STA maximum TX power from 802.11 Power Capability IE

Note: Channel, OperatingClass and LinkBandwidth reflect the AP radio
context (same for all STAs on that AP). ERP, MinTxPower and MaxTxPower
are STA-specific values from the association request frame.

MinTxPower and MaxTxPower are sourced from the 802.11 Power Capability
IE (EID=33) in the STA assoc request, exposed by hostapd wpa_ctrl as
min_txpower= and max_txpower= in the STA command response. This is the
standard nl80211/hostapd path — no vendor commands needed.

Fixed parameters (were returning wrong/zero values):
  VhtCapabilities          - parse vht_caps_info= from hostapd STA reply
  SignalStrength           - parse signal= from hostapd STA reply
  MaxDownlinkRateSupported - parse maxphyrate= from hostapd STA reply
  MaxUplinkRateSupported   - same source as MaxDownlinkRateSupported
  LinkBandwidth            - read pRadio->runningChannelBandwidth

Set assocCaps.linkBandwidthSetByDriver=true to prevent
wld_ad_syncCapabilities recalculating back to HT-cap bandwidth.

Signed-off-by: Jassim Shanavaskhan <jshanava@qti.qualcomm.com>
